    {
      "id": "claim_b4c79dcf786c4434ae6551385d83190e",
      "statement": "RestRedisCache reads REST_REDIS_URI (default http://localhost:8080) plus optional REST_REDIS_USERNAME and REST_REDIS_PASSWORD — blank values are treated as unset and the credentials are sent as HTTP Basic auth only when set — and applies the same fail-fast contract as RedisCache: a failed PING closes the client and throws IllegalStateException (\"Could not connect to Redis at <uri>\").",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/edu/kit/kastel/mcse/ardoco/llm/cache/RestRedisCache.java#L43-L68",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1d1fd2aac1ffce78f4c4cdc239d43f3cb7a9fa84151e62fa58f822449402e98f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_cb0d43fcca394f7387e9e55b5e4e30e6",
      "statement": "All cache configuration is read from the CacheManager's EnvironmentProvider at two distinct times: CACHE_HIERARCHY (default LOCAL) and CACHE_REPLACEMENT_STRATEGY (default NONE) are read once at construction, while the Redis connection settings are read when a cache is first requested via getCache — a manager configured for REDIS performs no network I/O until that first call. The cache directory is not an environment variable: it is set in code via CacheManager.setCacheDir (null selects the default \"cache\" directory, which is created if missing), and getDefaultInstance throws IllegalStateException until setCacheDir has been called.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/edu/kit/kastel/mcse/ardoco/llm/cache/CacheManager.java#L146-L148",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9c0e3ae5e609505e71cda669084e72095840e800387fd06be10ed336e0f4519a:"
