    {
      "id": "claim_f6f7195069d84673bc70caf37b5af94f",
      "statement": "The LOCAL layer keeps entries in memory and persists them atomically (temp file plus REPLACE_EXISTING copy) only on write(), auto-flushing solely once more than MAX_DIRTY (50) modifications have accumulated; CacheManager.flush() cascades to every cache it handed out, while the Redis-backed flush is a no-op because Redis persists immediately — so a run that relies on the local cache directory must end with an explicit CacheManager.flush().",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/edu/kit/kastel/mcse/ardoco/llm/cache/CacheManager.java#L294-L298",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:16c5918286a8d49303674f2f8757af63f44b5fe5ea0cf3d6d6fa478b8448f6ae:"
