    {
      "id": "claim_74a04d54e35e47488700547c66fba7af",
      "statement": "The LOCAL cache directory is the replication artifact: its JSON files are self-contained, so shipping the directory lets others reproduce a run offline (no API keys, no Redis, no model access) with CACHE_HIERARCHY=LOCAL. Running experiments with CACHE_HIERARCHY=REDIS,LOCAL (or REST_REDIS,LOCAL) fills it via write-through writes plus backfill of entries that exist only in the remote layer, and CacheManager.flush() at the end ensures everything is on disk before the directory is shipped.",
