    {
      "id": "claim_54bdd937381d44a5a59eb01bc7ab8fa3",
      "statement": "The cache's entire Redis interaction is limited to the operations exposed by the UnifiedRedisClient seam — ping, exists, hget, hset, and close — which both the Jedis-backed RedisAdapter and the REST-backed RestRedisAdapter implement; this is why the REST-Redis server only needs to proxy those few operations and a thin HTTP server suffices.",
