      "id": "claim_5a9e364e067d456e82b6e02cbd59cf90",
      "statement": "In a layered CACHE_HIERARCHY the backends are constructed in order at the first getCache call, so an unreachable REDIS still aborts cache acquisition even when LOCAL is also configured; pairing a remote backend with LOCAL provides data fallback and offline reproduction, not startup tolerance.",
